# Copy to apps/web/.env.production.local and adjust. `.env*` is gitignored;
# this file is committed as the template.
#
# Why this file exists: `next build` sets NODE_ENV=production and loads env
# files in this order, first match wins per variable:
#   .env.production.local  >  .env.local  >  .env.production  >  .env
# `.env.local` is also loaded by `next dev` and is where local dev keeps
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://localhost:3001. Without this file, a deploy
# build picks up THAT localhost value too (`next build` doesn't know it's
# "for production" any differently than `next dev` knows it's "for dev" —
# both just load .env.local) and ships a bundle that only works on the
# machine running the API. This file wins the lookup first, so the deploy
# build is always correct regardless of what .env.local currently says.
#
# Verify after building, before uploading:
#   grep -rl "localhost:3001" apps/web/out/_next/   → must be empty
#   grep -rl "api.pistora.se" apps/web/out/_next/    → must hit
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=https://api.pistora.se
